- Atomic filesystem replacement.
- Temporary-file handling.
- File flush and directory synchronization where supported.
- Crash recovery.
- Stale-operation reconciliation.
- Token replay prevention.
- Password-change supersession.
- Recovery after process termination.

If the existing architecture cannot guarantee these properties, explicitly state the limitation.

Do not invent transactional guarantees.

